    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look toward today\u2019s slate with a calculated focus on efficiency, as we navigate the scarcity of stolen bases in our 5x5 build. **Miguel Vargas** draws the start at 1B with a score of 46.45, buoyed primarily by his locked-in #3 spot in the batting order. While Messick presents a moderate challenge with a 3.51 xERA, **Miguel Vargas** retains value through his recent high-contact performance and the structural advantage of hitting in the heart of the order. We are proceeding cautiously, however, as we monitor for any late lineup shifts that might further compress his projected efficiency against this left-handed matchup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed our 40.0-point threshold with a score of 36.07. While his underlying metrics remain respectable, the combination of a tough matchup against Smith and a suppressed #9 spot in the batting order dropped his daily outlook below our minimum floor requirement. We are currently navigating a depleted roster with **Luis Robert Jr.** sidelined on the IL, while stalwarts like **Kyle Tucker** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** are inactive due to a team off-day. Consequently, our offensive ceiling is heavily contingent on our active contributors maintaining plate discipline; we will continue to monitor the status of secondary options like **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** to ensure we aren't leaving stolen base potential on the pine if a sudden defensive sub or platoon shift presents itself later in the day.",
